{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>With boils and with חרס.</b> The word חרס is a kind of dry mange that requires scraping (לחרס), and so it is written concerning the affliction of Job (Job 2:8): ״ויקח לו חרש להתגרד בו״ — and he took for himself a potsherd to scrape himself; so the commentators explained. But it is possible to interpret ובחרס from the word for sun (שמש), for He will strike them with the sun's plague, and it has three names: שמש, חמה, חרס. שמש — on account of its being a servant (עבד משמש) attending upon its Maker, and through the servant's virtue the Master's virtue becomes known; חמה — on account of heat (חמימות); חרס — because it was created to shine upon the earth. And furthermore, all three of them hint at the fourth great cycle, which is 365 days, and at the names of its two guides. And likewise regarding the three names of the moon, which are סהר, ירח, לבנה — but this is not the place to elaborate. But Scripture warns that if they do not hearken to the voice of the Blessed One, He will strike them with the sun's plague, which is the corruption of the air and the elements, and this is ובחרס from the word (Job 9:7): ״האומר לחרס ולא יזרח״ — Who says to the sun and it does not shine; and likewise (Judges 14:18): ״בטרם יבא החרסה״ — before the sun came. And behold, this is the opposite of what David, peace be upon him, mentioned in the blessing (Psalms 121:6): ״יומם השמש לא יככה וירח בלילה״ — The sun shall not smite you by day, nor the moon by night; corresponding to this it says here יככה — shall smite you, for illnesses come by way of foods and the change of the air in lands, and all is through the sun's motion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The prooftexts he cites as (שם ט) and (שופטים י״ד:י״ח) refer back to Job (איוב) in context; שם ט is Job 9:7 and the Judges citation is 14:18, normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:45.250223678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}